  "summary": "Pablo Picasso, born in Málaga on 25 October 1881, moved to France permanently in 1904 and lived in the Bateau-Lavoir studio in Montmartre, Paris. He developed Cubism with Georges Braque and painted Guernica in the Grands Augustins studio. He died in Mougins on 8 April 1973.",
